WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.557
Now it is your turn to build the workflow.

00:00:02.557 --> 00:00:05.517
The starter Data frame is already provided.

00:00:05.517 --> 00:00:10.167
Your task is to complete the missing Pandas steps.

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:13.172
First, convert the date column to datetime.

00:00:13.172 --> 00:00:16.837
Then keep orders with an amount of at least fifty.

00:00:16.837 --> 00:00:21.857
Create an order-size category using the ranges shown in the instructions.

00:00:21.857 --> 00:00:29.919
After that, group the data by region and calculate total sales, average order amount, and the number of orders.

00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:34.191
There is intentionally no completed solution on this slide.

00:00:34.191 --> 00:00:39.316
Use the earlier examples as patterns, but write the workflow yourself.

00:00:39.316 --> 00:00:45.536
I recommend running your code after each major step instead of writing everything at once.

00:00:45.536 --> 00:00:49.826
For example, first confirm that the date conversion works.

00:00:49.826 --> 00:00:53.831
Then check the filtering. Then inspect the categories.

00:00:53.831 --> 00:00:56.581
Finally, build the grouped summary.

00:00:56.581 --> 00:01:02.531
As an extension, sort the final table from the highest total sales to the lowest.

00:01:02.531 --> 00:01:07.601
The goal is not only to get an answer, but to build a workflow that you can explain.
